hived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2025-06-30T16:54:12Z","updated_at":"2025-06-30T19:55:03Z","closed_at":"2025-06-30T19:54:55Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Not reproducible in: 4.1.4.stable.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta1 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon(TM) Vega 8 Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 27.20.1028.1) - AMD Ryzen 5 3500U with Radeon Vega Mobile Gfx (8 threads) - 9.87 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm that guy again from 4.1 that recently moved to 4.5, I'm enjoying it! But found another bug that I gotta report.\n\nFor some reason I'm getting paths that look like this:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c1d10631-90f5-4cdd-bd52-e8bf072a37ee)\n\nIf I move the target position a bit to the left it looks like this:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a886bca4-c1a2-444e-964a-b90925c2c39a)\n\nIn 4.1 it would never take that link to the top as it would always be the longer path, I haven't followed navigation changes between the versions but I'm pretty sure this is a bug.\n\nIn the MRP the mouse position is the agent's target position and you can change the parent node's position to test other paths.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Make a scene with some navigation regions and links of different shapes.\n- Add a navigation agent and test what path it takes.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[pathfinding-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20984253/pathfinding-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0",